\\left(x\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671087 1080 "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)" 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671087 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671087 1083 #uuid "288156d7-fbae-55ec-bd81-8d26b011bb58" 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671088 1080 "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)" 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671088 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671088 1083 #uuid "2cdbbe3c-eec3-59a6-b054-5cec462a5469" 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671089 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671108 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671089 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671089 1071 "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y = y(x)$:\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\cdot y=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}$\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x)) = I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671089 1072 #uuid "34ac2e02-a12f-5cc4-8239-e8e5387b0f1f" 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671089 1074 "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=- \\frac{5}{2}$ and $Q(x)=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(- \\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671090 1080 "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{\\frac{8 x}{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{\\frac{8 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)" 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671090 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671090 1083 #uuid "37fd9fa0-313a-5948-869a-7bb48ef556ca" 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671091 1080 "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)" 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671091 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671091 1083 #uuid "41263caa-37d4-5894-bdd4-055b030643a5" 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671092 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671084 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671092 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538655 17592186045443 true] [17592186671092 1071 "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\